// One mistake, however many parameters follow it. Reported once per later
// parameter, a single misplaced `..` produced sixty identical diagnostics — a
// cascade, which is what the 25-error bound exists to contain and could not,
// because that bound is only consulted where a diagnostic aborts the parse.
fn f(..a, b, c, d, e, g, h) { a }
print(1)
